{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory opens with a family asking about danger and medication correctness. The doctor immediately initiates a comprehensive workspace query and, upon receiving only record indices, delivers a lengthy response that includes acute red-flag screening (RC1 met), contextual interpretation (RC2 met), information-gap handling (RC3 met), medication safety boundary (RC4 met), transfer/handoff safety (RC5 met), and an executable next step with family receipt (RC6 met). The model stays within its role and does not fabricate (RC7 met). Multiple high-order points are triggered and actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact: HO1 (correction of 'SpO2 97% means safe' misconception with teach-back), HO3 (verification of vital signs timing/source via targeted questions), and HO4 (tailored transfer checklist amid family paperwork fatigue). No responsibility-chain errors were committed. All dimensions are at least good. The closure is safe, traceable, and valid as the family explicitly confirms understanding and intended actions. The trajectory thus satisfies Strong and meets the Perfect threshold via multiple completed high-order points.",
